  "title": "Fog Fix Legacy",
  "description": "Renders fog via GLSL, enabling round fog support for AMD and Intel GPU users.",
  "body": "Renders fog via GLSL, enabling round fog support for AMD and Intel GPU users. By default, Minecraft in older versions required the GL_NV_fog_distance extension to have rounded fog, otherwise it rendered flat. Flat fog is the one that makes elements in the corners of the screen visible but not when you look at them, while round fog does not do that.\n\nWith mod:\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\">\n  <tr style=\"border: none;\">\n    <td style=\"width: 50%; padding: 4px; border: none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/e645e76a551a872fe9b08dee92929a6d5807b466_0.webp\" alt=\"The fog is rounded, in an area with a extreme hills biome and a jungle.\" style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;\">\n    </td>\n    <td style=\"width: 50%; padding: 4px; border: none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/4af30c66bf3674c7fd560f446500f7ec95fb182f_0.webp\" alt=\"The fog is rounded, on a superflat world with a village.\" style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;\">\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>\n\nWithout mod:\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\">\n  <tr style=\"border: none;\">\n    <td style=\"width: 50%; padding: 4px; border: none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/4764f9289d691d61784ccb40ab6f526ed0b7713c_0.webp\" alt=\"The fog is flat, in an area with a extreme hills biome and a jungle.\" style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;\">\n    </td>\n    <td style=\"width: 50%; padding: 4px; border: none;\">\n      <img src=\"https://cdn.modrinth.com/data/cached_images/48ba93e297af4d032c742f83829969a93abced93_0.webp\" alt=\"The fog is flat, on a superflat world with a village.\" style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;\">\n    </td>\n  </tr>\n</table>",
